<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-002-AL9>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-002-AL9" ;
  triage:title "AL.9 M5 cross-host disposition unauthorized — sprint doc only allows SHA-reuse-from-AL.7 or documented rerun, branch drops the row to an unassigned future secure-connector instead" ;
  triage:description "req-qa (AL9-QA-1, 2026-08-07) flags that AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md/AL9-proof-subject.md/AL9-cutover-table.md currently record the M5/cross-host row as dropped/deferred to a future secure connector, which does not match either allowed sprint-doc disposition (reuse AL.7's pinned M5 artifact by SHA, or re-run and record the triggering diff). IMPORTANT CONTEXT for the triage agent: this dropped-row state reflects an EARLIER team-lead directive (drop the row entirely, defer to a later secure connector) that has since been PARTIALLY REVERSED by a follow-up team-lead directive authorizing arch-ctm to build a minimal, curl-testable, non-loopback-capable M5 connector (explicitly not a new state machine or config-layering abstraction) to produce real M5 evidence. arch-ctm ACK'd this reversal but has NOT YET pushed the corresponding code/doc changes to this branch as of 9b4c4799. Record this finding as open at current HEAD, but flag in the record's notes/description that resolution is already in flight via a separate, already-dispatched dev instruction (not yet landed) rather than requiring a fresh dev decision. RECHECK (QA-AL9-RECHECK-1, 2026-08-07): still open, correctly so. At integrate/phase-al@dc9c7197 the row's disposition text has changed to 'Documented rerun required' with a fully specified rerun procedure (real cross-host env-var config, curl-based POST, expected evidence to record) -- the originally-cited 'Dropped / deferred' text no longer reproduces. However, the sprint doc's acceptance criterion demands the artifact be 'captured' (an executed result), not merely 'documented' as a procedure -- so the underlying gap is unresolved. arch-ctm confirmed a same-host loopback-alias simulation would not satisfy genuine cross-host proof and declined to fabricate one, escalating to team-lead for M5-team coordination instead (parallel to the already-escalated HOSTFLAG-SPEC-GAP-AL9). Quality-mgr independently confirmed the current row text and agrees the escalation, not a loopback substitute, is the correct call. Remains open, blocked on real M5-team execution. INDEPENDENT REVIEW (quality-mgr, 2026-08-10, integrate/phase-al@fc73d4ec / PR #824): the finding's specific complaint was that the M5 row's disposition matched neither allowed sprint-doc option (SHA-reuse or documented-and-recorded rerun) and had no owner/trigger. PR #824 (docs-only, verified via gh pr diff: AL9-physical-proof-matrix.md +3/-3, sprint-AL9-physical-proof-ledger-freeze.md +23/-0) changes the M5 row's disposition to 'Final-candidate physical proof pending; no AL.7 reuse is claimed', names team-lead as evidence-pass owner and arch-ctm as the M5 execution operator, and ties execution to an explicit trigger (frozen final integrate/phase-al candidate SHA, before proposing to develop) recorded in the new sprint-doc section. This is now a fully authorized, owned, and triggered disposition consistent with the sprint doc's allowed options -- the specific defect this finding tracked (unauthorized/unowned/unscheduled disposition) is resolved. The underlying M5 artifact is still not captured; that is expected and correctly deferred to the final integration->develop evidence pass per the user's standing no-new-smoke-tests-until-final-review constraint, and is no longer this finding's concern -- it is covered by the new final-evidence-pass process itself and by the still-open ATM-QA-004-AL9 for the write-path evidence class generally. Closing this finding on that basis." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
